    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "CLASS VARIABLES\n\nVariables live on the class, so each instance keeps its own copy for as long as it exists.\nAdd them in the Variables panel (name, type, default). Drag one into the graph to get a\nGET node (a pure value) or a SET node (an exec node that stores a value).\nTypes used here: i64 (whole number), f64 (decimal), bool, String.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          190.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "1. SET WITH A LITERAL\nSet counter: the Value pin is not wired, so the number typed on the node (41) is stored.",
        "position": [
          360.0,
          -50.0
        ],
        "size": [
          270.0,
          100.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "s1"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "2. READ-MODIFY-WRITE\nGet counter -> Add (+1) -> Set counter. The classic increment: read the variable, compute, store it back.",
        "position": [
          360.0,
          320.0
        ],
        "size": [
          840.0,
          100.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
          0.55,
          0.15,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "gc",
          "inc",
          "s2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-4",
        "text": "3. BOOLEANS\nNot flips true to false; alive ends up false.",
        "position": [
          960.0,
          490.0
        ],
        "size": [
          640.0,
          80.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.6,
          0.3,
          0.75,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "ga",
          "neg",
          "s3"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-5",
        "text": "4. TEXT\nString Concat joins two strings: \"Pulsar\" + \"!\".",
        "position": [
          1260.0,
          660.0
        ],
        "size": [
          640.0,
          80.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "gn",
          "bang",
          "s4"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-6",
        "text": "5. SHOW IT\nThe counter (an integer) is wired straight into Print String: it is converted to text for you. Expect \"42\".",
        "position": [
          1860.0,
          490.0
        ],
        "size": [
          560.0,
          100.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.55,
